/* book exam traps: Writing VM = VDD/2 for every inverter. It holds only when kn = kp and Vtn = |Vtp|; with equal widths the stronger nMOS pulls VM down. | Writing the pMOS overdrive as Vin − |Vtp|. Its source sits at VDD, so the overdrive is VDD − Vin − |Vtp|. | Taking VIL and VIH as the thresholds Vtn and VDD − |Vtp|. They are the points where the slope is −1, inside regions B and D. | Swapping the margin formulas. NMH = VOH − VIH and NML = VIL − VOL; logic swing VOH − VOL is a different, larger number. */
