/* book: lead: An NMOS inverter is one nMOS driver that pulls the output down plus a load that pulls it up. The driver alone cannot make a logic 1, so the load sets the high level, and because the load is still on when the driver pulls down, the low level is a tug-of-war between the two. Four loads are standard: a resistor, an enhancement nMOS with its gate at VDD, a depletion nMOS with its gate tied to its sour */
