/* book Worked example 2: Q: An enhancement-load inverter has VDD = 5 V, Vt = 0.8 V for both transistors (ignore body effect), kL = 20 µA/V² and kD = 180 µA/V² (ratio 9). Find VOH, VOL and the static current at the low output.
   1. VOH = VDD − Vt = 5 − 0.8 = 4.2 V.
   2. At Vin = 5 V the load is saturated and the driver linear: (20/2)(4.2 − VOL)² = 180[4.2VOL − VOL²/2] (currents in µA).
   3. Divide by 10: (4.2 − VOL)² = 18(4.2VOL − VOL²/2) = 75.6VOL − 9VOL². Expand: 17.64 − 8.4VOL + VOL² = 75.6VOL − 9VOL², so 10VOL² − 84VOL + 17.64 = 0.
   4. VOL = (84 − √(7056 − 705.6))/20 = (84 − 79.69)/20 = 0.216 V.
   5. Current = 10 µA/V² × (4.2 − 0.216)² = 10 × 15.88 = 159 µA, so 0.79 mW at 5 V.
   Answer: VOH = 4.2 V (lower still with body effect), VOL ≈ 0.22 V, and 159 µA flows while the output is low. */
