/* book exam traps: Using the saturation equation for the driver at the low output. VDS = VOL is far below VGS − Vtn, so the driver is linear. | Giving VOH = VDD for the enhancement load. It stops one threshold short, and the body effect makes that threshold larger than Vt0. | Calling a depletion load off because VGS = 0. Its threshold is negative, so it conducts until VDS = 0. | Taking the supply side as the source of an nMOS load. Its source is the output, so its VGS and VSB follow the output. */
