/* book exam traps: Swapping tPHL and tPLH. tPHL is the output falling, set by the nMOS and caused by a rising input. | Dropping the 2 in CLVDD/(2IDsat). Delay ends at the 50% point, so only half the swing is moved. | Squaring VDD instead of the overdrive VDD − Vtn in the saturation current. | Calling rise time a delay. Rise time is measured on the output alone; delay is from input to output. | Unit slips: fF × V = fC and fC ÷ µA = ns. Keep fF with µA and read nanoseconds. */
